**Code Explanation:**

The code performs the requested data integrity and sanity checks on the Eulerian cascade and Lagrangian Kraichnan datasets. First, it loads the raw cascade datasets and the corresponding scale array. To verify the K41 cascade scaling, the velocity increments are normalized by their overall root-mean-square (RMS) velocity. The structure functions S_p(r) = <|delta_u|^p> are computed for moments p=1 to 6. The scaling exponents zeta_p are extracted by performing a linear regression of log(S_p) versus log(r) within the inertial range (excluding the boundary scales). The computed exponents are printed alongside the theoretical K41 predictions (zeta_p = p/3). Second, the code loads the Kraichnan single-particle trajectory data for xi=1.0 and its corresponding time grid. Since the trajectory data has 4001 points and the full time grid has 10001 points, a linearly spaced time array is constructed to correctly align with the trajectory steps. The Mean Squared Displacement (MSD) is computed by averaging the squared displacements over all realizations. The scaling exponent H is extracted by fitting log(MSD) versus log(t) in the asymptotic regime (the second half of the trajectory). The computed H is printed and compared to the theoretical expectation H = xi/2 = 0.5. The raw data files are only read and not overwritten, ensuring they are preserved for subsequent steps.

